{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011dd3HHiYgox1pwYWqaybdM","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Current Evaluation State\n     2→\n     3→## Active Text\n     4→- **Name:** cask_of_amontillado\n     5→- **Attempt:** 1\n     6→- **Phase:** awaiting_analysis\n     7→- **baseline_score:** 6.10\n     8→\n     9→## Latest Scores\n    10→- Structure Detection: 9/10\n    11→- Character Extraction: 4/10 ← CRITICAL FAILURE\n    12→- Character Profiles: 4/10 ← CRITICAL FAILURE\n    13→- Chapter Summaries: 6/10\n    14→- Pronunciation Guide: 7/10\n    15→- HTML Presentation: 8/10\n    16→- **Overall: 6.10/10** (threshold: 8.0)\n    17→\n    18→## Current Issues (Priority Order)\n    19→\n    20→### CRITICAL\n    21→\n    22→1. **\"Amontillado\" (a wine) is listed as a character**\n    23→   - Problem: The analysis created a character entry for \"Amontillado\" which is the Spanish sherry wine, NOT a person\n    24→   - Evidence: `characters[0].canonical_name` = \"Amontillado\" with 16 mentions\n    25→   - The description text is actually describing Montresor (the narrator) but attributed to the wine name\n    26→   - Location: Likely `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` - NER or LLM extraction is treating the title word as a character\n    27→   - Root cause: The word \"Amontillado\" appears frequently in the text (34 times) as part of dialogue about the wine, and the system incorrectly identified it as a character name\n    28→   - Fix approach: Add filtering to exclude common nouns/objects that appear in titles from character extraction, or improve the LLM prompt to distinguish between characters and objects\n    29→\n    30→2. **Montresor NOT identified as narrator**\n    31→   - Problem: `is_narrator: false` for Montresor, but he IS the first-person narrator\n    32→   - Evidence: The story opens with \"I had borne as I best could\" and continues in first person throughout\n    33→   - The `plot_summary` incorrectly calls the narrator \"Amontillado\" instead of Montresor\n    34→   - Location: Likely `src/agents/summary_agent.py` or narrator detection logic\n    35→   - Fix approach: Narrator detection should look for first-person pronouns and identify which character uses \"I\"\n    36→\n    37→3. **Montresor has NO profile content**\n    38→   - Problem: Montresor has zero descriptions, zero evidence, zero personality/voice guidance\n    39→   - Evidence: `characters[2]` (Montresor) has empty `descriptions`, `relationships`, `evidence` arrays\n    40→   - Only 1 mention_count when he should be the most mentioned character (as the narrator)\n    41→   - Location: Character extraction is failing to associate the narrator's actions with Montresor\n    42→   - Fix approach: Improve narrator-to-character linking - when a character is identified as narrator, their profile should be built from all first-person statements\n    43→\n    44→### HIGH\n    45→\n    46→4. **Luchresi missing from character list**\n    47→   - Problem: Luchresi is mentioned 6 times by name but not included in characters\n    48→   - Evidence: He appears in dialogue as a rival wine expert that Montresor uses to manipulate Fortunato\n    49→   - Location: Character extraction may be filtering by mention count or missing this name\n    50→   - Fix approach: Lower threshold or improve detection - he's clearly a named character\n    51→\n    52→5. **Plot summary uses \"Amontillado\" as narrator name**\n    53→   - Problem: The `overview.plot_summary.plot_summary` field repeatedly says \"Amontillado recounts...\" and \"Amontillado leads Fortunato...\"\n    54→   - Evidence: This is a downstream effect of issue #1 - the summary agent used the wrong character as narrator\n    55→   - Location: `src/agents/summary_agent.py`\n    56→   - Fix approach: Fixing issue #1 and #2 should cascade to fix this\n    57→\n    58→### MEDIUM\n    59→\n    60→6. **Some pronunciation false positives**\n    61→   - Problem: Common words like \"jingled\", \"filmy\", \"orbs\", \"leer\" flagged unnecessarily\n    62→   - Evidence: 56 total pronunciations flagged, some are common English words\n    63→   - Location: `src/pipeline/pronunciation/` or pronunciation agent\n    64→   - Fix approach: Add word frequency filtering (as noted in ATTEMPT_1_SUMMARY.md)\n    65→\n    66→7. **\"Medoc\" not flagged for pronunciation**\n    67→   - Problem: French wine region name not in pronunciation guide\n    68→   - Evidence: Appears in text (\"a draught of the Medoc\", \"My own fancy grew warm with the Medoc\")\n    69→   - Location: Pronunciation detection\n    70→   - Fix approach: Minor - improve foreign word detection\n    71→\n    72→## Fix History\n    73→\n    74→### Attempt 1 (2026-01-18): Fixed validator heuristic for non-person entities\n    75→\n    76→**Root Cause Analysis:**\n    77→- Issue #1 (\"Amontillado as character\"):\n    78→  - Traced from: `output/cask_of_amontillado/analysis.json` → `CharacterMap.characters[0]` → `CharacterExtractionPipeline` → `CharacterValidator._heuristic_validation()` line 167\n    79→  - **Root cause:** Heuristic at line 167-178 auto-accepted any name with 10+ mentions and 3+ dialogue occurrences WITHOUT LLM validation\n    80→  - \"Amontillado\" (wine) had 16 mentions and appeared in dialogue (\"Amontillado!\" when discussing the wine), triggering false acceptance\n    81→  - Confidence: HIGH\n    82→\n    83→- Issue #2 (Montresor not narrator):\n    84→  - **Root cause:** Cascading failure from Issue #1\n    85→  - Narrator detector received corrupted character list with \"Amontillado\" (16 mentions) vs \"Montresor\" (1 mention)\n    86→  - LLM picked \"Amontillado\" as narrator due to higher prominence\n    87→  - Confidence: HIGH\n    88→\n    89→- Issue #3 (Montresor missing profile):\n    90→  - **Root cause:** NER limitation - \"Montresor\" name appears only once explicitly in text (when Fortunato cries \"For the love of God, Montresor!\")\n    91→  - All first-person narration uses \"I\", \"my\" which NER doesn't attribute to Montresor\n    92→  - Confidence: HIGH (fundamental NER limitation, requires different approach to fix)\n    93→\n    94→**Changes Made:**\n    95→- File: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/validator.py`\n    96→- Line 165-178: **Removed** overly aggressive heuristic that auto-accepted high-mention-count names without LLM validation\n    97→- Line 39-54: **Enhanced** validation system prompt to explicitly reject objects, food, drink, places\n    98→- Line 66-69: **Enhanced** validation prompt template to ask LLM to distinguish between people and objects being discussed\n    99→\n   100→**Smoke Test Results (PASS):**\n   101→- Ran analysis on \"The Cask of Amontillado - Poe.txt\" with qwen2.5:32b\n   102→- ✅ \"Amontillado\" removed from character list (went from 3 to 2 characters)\n   103→- ✅ Narrator correctly identified as \"Montresor\" in plot summary\n   104→- ✅ Plot summary says \"The story is narrated by Montresor\" (not \"Amontillado\")\n   105→- ❌ Montresor still has only 1 mention (NER limitation - deferred as separate issue)\n   106→\n   107→**Full Test Suite: PASSED**\n   108→- 444 tests passed, 11 skipped, 1 warning\n   109→- No regressions introduced\n   110→\n   111→**Issues Addressed:**\n   112→- ✅ Issue #1: Fixed (Amontillado no longer extracted as character)\n   113→- ✅ Issue #2: Fixed (Montresor correctly identified as narrator in plot summary)\n   114→- ✅ Issue #5: Fixed (plot summary now uses \"Montresor\" not \"Amontillado\")\n   115→- ⏸️ Issue #3: Partially addressed (narrator identified but profile still thin due to 1 mention - NER limitation)\n   116→\n   117→## Next Action\n   118→**Phase:** awaiting_analysis\n   119→\n   120→Re-run analysis on cask_of_amontillado to verify fix improves quality score.\n   121→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f608c3a-7e81-4986-9423-3d743ad64945","uuid":"c36641c4-95eb-44a8-8312-4bb4e7d502ff","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/EVALUATION_STATE.md","content":"# Current Evaluation State\n\n## Active Text\n- **Name:** cask_of_amontillado\n- **Attempt:** 1\n- **Phase:** awaiting_analysis\n- **baseline_score:** 6.10\n\n## Latest Scores\n- Structure Detection: 9/10\n- Character Extraction: 4/10 ← CRITICAL FAILURE\n- Character Profiles: 4/10 ← CRITICAL FAILURE\n- Chapter Summaries: 6/10\n- Pronunciation Guide: 7/10\n- HTML Presentation: 8/10\n- **Overall: 6.10/10** (threshold: 8.0)\n\n## Current Issues (Priority Order)\n\n### CRITICAL\n\n1. **\"Amontillado\" (a wine) is listed as a character**\n   - Problem: The analysis created a character entry for \"Amontillado\" which is the Spanish sherry wine, NOT a person\n   - Evidence: `characters[0].canonical_name` = \"Amontillado\" with 16 mentions\n   - The description text is actually describing Montresor (the narrator) but attributed to the wine name\n   - Location: Likely `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` - NER or LLM extraction is treating the title word as a character\n   - Root cause: The word \"Amontillado\" appears frequently in the text (34 times) as part of dialogue about the wine, and the system incorrectly identified it as a character name\n   - Fix approach: Add filtering to exclude common nouns/objects that appear in titles from character extraction, or improve the LLM prompt to distinguish between characters and objects\n\n2. **Montresor NOT identified as narrator**\n   - Problem: `is_narrator: false` for Montresor, but he IS the first-person narrator\n   - Evidence: The story opens with \"I had borne as I best could\" and continues in first person throughout\n   - The `plot_summary` incorrectly calls the narrator \"Amontillado\" instead of Montresor\n   - Location: Likely `src/agents/summary_agent.py` or narrator detection logic\n   - Fix approach: Narrator detection should look for first-person pronouns and identify which character uses \"I\"\n\n3. **Montresor has NO profile content**\n   - Problem: Montresor has zero descriptions, zero evidence, zero personality/voice guidance\n   - Evidence: `characters[2]` (Montresor) has empty `descriptions`, `relationships`, `evidence` arrays\n   - Only 1 mention_count when he should be the most mentioned character (as the narrator)\n   - Location: Character extraction is failing to associate the narrator's actions with Montresor\n   - Fix approach: Improve narrator-to-character linking - when a character is identified as narrator, their profile should be built from all first-person statements\n\n### HIGH\n\n4. **Luchresi missing from character list**\n   - Problem: Luchresi is mentioned 6 times by name but not included in characters\n   - Evidence: He appears in dialogue as a rival wine expert that Montresor uses to manipulate Fortunato\n   - Location: Character extraction may be filtering by mention count or missing this name\n   - Fix approach: Lower threshold or improve detection - he's clearly a named character\n\n5. **Plot summary uses \"Amontillado\" as narrator name**\n   - Problem: The `overview.plot_summary.plot_summary` field repeatedly says \"Amontillado recounts...\" and \"Amontillado leads Fortunato...\"\n   - Evidence: This is a downstream effect of issue #1 - the summary agent used the wrong character as narrator\n   - Location: `src/agents/summary_agent.py`\n   - Fix approach: Fixing issue #1 and #2 should cascade to fix this\n\n### MEDIUM\n\n6. **Some pronunciation false positives**\n   - Problem: Common words like \"jingled\", \"filmy\", \"orbs\", \"leer\" flagged unnecessarily\n   - Evidence: 56 total pronunciations flagged, some are common English words\n   - Location: `src/pipeline/pronunciation/` or pronunciation agent\n   - Fix approach: Add word frequency filtering (as noted in ATTEMPT_1_SUMMARY.md)\n\n7. **\"Medoc\" not flagged for pronunciation**\n   - Problem: French wine region name not in pronunciation guide\n   - Evidence: Appears in text (\"a draught of the Medoc\", \"My own fancy grew warm with the Medoc\")\n   - Location: Pronunciation detection\n   - Fix approach: Minor - improve foreign word detection\n\n## Fix History\n\n### Attempt 1 (2026-01-18): Fixed validator heuristic for non-person entities\n\n**Root Cause Analysis:**\n- Issue #1 (\"Amontillado as character\"):\n  - Traced from: `output/cask_of_amontillado/analysis.json` → `CharacterMap.characters[0]` → `CharacterExtractionPipeline` → `CharacterValidator._heuristic_validation()` line 167\n  - **Root cause:** Heuristic at line 167-178 auto-accepted any name with 10+ mentions and 3+ dialogue occurrences WITHOUT LLM validation\n  - \"Amontillado\" (wine) had 16 mentions and appeared in dialogue (\"Amontillado!\" when discussing the wine), triggering false acceptance\n  - Confidence: HIGH\n\n- Issue #2 (Montresor not narrator):\n  - **Root cause:** Cascading failure from Issue #1\n  - Narrator detector received corrupted character list with \"Amontillado\" (16 mentions) vs \"Montresor\" (1 mention)\n  - LLM picked \"Amontillado\" as narrator due to higher prominence\n  - Confidence: HIGH\n\n- Issue #3 (Montresor missing profile):\n  - **Root cause:** NER limitation - \"Montresor\" name appears only once explicitly in text (when Fortunato cries \"For the love of God, Montresor!\")\n  - All first-person narration uses \"I\", \"my\" which NER doesn't attribute to Montresor\n  - Confidence: HIGH (fundamental NER limitation, requires different approach to fix)\n\n**Changes Made:**\n- File: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/validator.py`\n- Line 165-178: **Removed** overly aggressive heuristic that auto-accepted high-mention-count names without LLM validation\n- Line 39-54: **Enhanced** validation system prompt to explicitly reject objects, food, drink, places\n- Line 66-69: **Enhanced** validation prompt template to ask LLM to distinguish between people and objects being discussed\n\n**Smoke Test Results (PASS):**\n- Ran analysis on \"The Cask of Amontillado - Poe.txt\" with qwen2.5:32b\n- ✅ \"Amontillado\" removed from character list (went from 3 to 2 characters)\n- ✅ Narrator correctly identified as \"Montresor\" in plot summary\n- ✅ Plot summary says \"The story is narrated by Montresor\" (not \"Amontillado\")\n- ❌ Montresor still has only 1 mention (NER limitation - deferred as separate issue)\n\n**Full Test Suite: PASSED**\n- 444 tests passed, 11 skipped, 1 warning\n- No regressions introduced\n\n**Issues Addressed:**\n- ✅ Issue #1: Fixed (Amontillado no longer extracted as character)\n- ✅ Issue #2: Fixed (Montresor correctly identified as narrator in plot summary)\n- ✅ Issue #5: Fixed (plot summary now uses \"Montresor\" not \"Amontillado\")\n- ⏸️ Issue #3: Partially addressed (narrator identified but profile still thin due to 1 mention - NER limitation)\n\n## Next Action\n**Phase:** awaiting_analysis\n\nRe-run analysis on cask_of_amontillado to verify fix improves quality score.\n","numLines":121,"startLine":1,"totalLines":121}}}
